# SEO and semantic structure

## Metadata by stack

- **Next.js App Router**: Use `metadata` or `async generateMetadata` per route: `title`, `description`, `metadataBase`, Open Graph/Twitter, `alternates.canonical` when applicable. Keep titles unique per route; avoid empty or duplicate descriptions. See @apps/nextjs-portfolio/app/layout.tsx for site-wide defaults and Sanity-driven settings.
- **Astro**: Set `<title>` and meta description via layout or frontmatter; use `@astrojs/sitemap` / RSS where the project already configures them.
- **TanStack Start / others**: Use that framework’s head/meta APIs for title, description, and share images.

## HTML and URLs

- Clear outline: `h1` for the main page topic when appropriate, then `h2` / `h3` without skipping levels.
- Use landmarks (`main`, `nav`, `header`, `footer`) once per page pattern; avoid multiple `main` unless documented by the framework.
- Prefer stable, human-readable URLs and slugs for new routes.

```tsx
import type { Metadata } from 'next';

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: 'Page title',
  description: 'Unique, concise summary for search and social previews.',
};
```
